hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan today  mansion a question from one of our  newsletter readers avi Nash who wrote  insane hi Evan I love your emails and I  read them carefully I'm a student of mba  program and i also want to be an  entrepreneur i want to start a one-stop  shop graphics and animation studio as my  life ambition but it'll take me a long  time to get some experience in the field  so i want your suggestions for young  entrepreneurs thank you avinash so  thanks for the question great question I  think the very first step for any  entrepreneur who wants to get started is  to figure out what type of business that  they want to run and you always want to  build it around something you're really  passionate about and so it sounds like  you you've probably found that so if you  have that's great whether it is you know  creating this animation studio or doing  something completely different you want  to make sure you're building a business  around something that you're really  passionate about helping people with the  next step that I usually recommend is go  out and work for somebody else has  already done it and so this could be  where your next step is if you're you  know graduating your program and you  know you're not ready to start up your  own business quite yet but you want to  learn a little bit more about it go work  for somebody who's already done what  you're trying to do is one of the  fastest ways to learn so go find  somebody who has a small business so  somebody who's say 10 employees whose in  exactly the same field that you want to  do and go learn from them and get  involved try to do more than whatever  you know your job description is  entrepreneurs always need help and if  you can you know be a keener and show  that you're really interested in eager  and want to learn from them then they'll  give you extra tasks even if it's you  know not paid for those extra tasks or  you're working extra hours you're doing  it because you want to learn right if  you're going to take a job you wanted to  teach you something and not just do it  for the money and I look at it this way  you're you're being paid to learn about  your industry so instead of going out  and trying it yourself and probably  failing because you don't know what  you're doing yet you go work for  somebody else has already done it you're  learning from their mistakes and if  you're making mistakes it's on somebody  else's dime so they're paying you to  make mistakes and they're paying you to  learn about the industry and so it will  do two things  it'll teach you about the industry it'll  give you contacts it'll tell you you  know what you're doing if it's right if  it's wrong you know the the insider  tricks well what kind of team you need  to have how to go out and get customers  all those things and so the more you can  get involved in the whole business and  approach the entrepreneur and see you  want it you want more responsibility you  want to get more involved the more you  can learn from them about the business  then the more success you know you'll  probably have because you've learned on  somebody else's dime but also it'll tell  you if you really want to do this  business or not and often entrepreneurs  get started in the business and I  realized I was just too much work or  this isn't what I thought it was going  to be and they lose a lot of money and  time and have to shut down and there  you're frustrated and then in debt and  so by going to work for somebody else is  already doing what you want to do it'll  give you the understanding of what that  business is like and you know you can  look at that entrepreneurs life you know  do you like how they live their life do  you like their lifestyle and the hours  are working and the type of things that  they're producing is that the life that  you want and it may be yeah that's an  awesome life I want that or no that's  crazy i didn't i didn't think it would  be this much work or it wasn't what I  thought it was and so again you're  learning while getting paid and they'll  tell you that's the right business to do  or not and so that's usually my  recommendation for getting started first  find something you're really passionate  about that you feel you can help other  people out a lot of value to their lives  and then try to go find somebody who's  already done what you're trying to do a  smallish company 10 employees or so  where you can really learn the industry  get some experience get some contacts  and see if it's something that you want  to do or not before you go out and  launch your own business and when you do  you'll have a lot of the experience that  you'll need by working because you've  worked for that other company so  hopefully that helps is your next step  up in osh good luck with finishing your  program and launching your own business  for those are you watching if you liked  it please give it a thumbs up below  makes you want to do more these videos  for you and you have a question about  your business feel free to leave it in  the comments below I always read those  and I try to respond to all of them if I  can so thank you and I'll see you in the  next episode  you
 

